<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton exporters seek tax exemption.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton exporters seek tax exemption.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani dealers urged the government on Sunday to exempt cotton exports from a 10 percent sales tax to enable them to buy and export some two million 375-lb bales of unsold stocks at ginneries.</p>
<p>The tax, which raises the cost of cotton, has hindered exports, which plunged to 17,129 bales between September 1 and December 22 from 1.747 million in the year-ago period, Maqbool Sadiq, chairman of the private Karachi Cotton Association said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The levy of sales tax is causing a serious setback to exports,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
